1. Where the detention period of a detainee exceeds 20 months from the date on which detention commenced;
2. Where, prior to obtaining approval from the Immigration Detention Review Committee for an extension of the period of detention, the period of detention under the main clause exceeds 3 months.
(3) Where the head of the competent Regional Immigration Service fails to obtain approval from the Immigration Detention Review Committee for the extension of the period of detention with respect to a detainee under paragraph (1), he or she shall lift the detention without delay.
(4) Where the head of the competent Regional Immigration Service applies to the Immigration Detention Review Committee for approval of an extension of the period of detention between June 1 and June 30, 2025, with respect to a detainee whose period of detention under the former Article 63 is less than 6 months at the time this Act enters into force, the person concerned may continue to be detained until such approval is obtained, but not beyond July 31, 2025.
Article 6 (Transitional measures concerning objections to detention)
(1) Where an objection to detention has been filed with the Minister of Justice pursuant to the former Article 55 at the time this Act enters into force, the former provisions shall apply.
(2) Where the former provisions apply pursuant to paragraph (1), no request for review of detention may be filed again with the Immigration Detention Review Committee with respect to the same matters.
Article 7 (Transitional measures concerning approval for continued detention)
Where approval by the Minister of Justice under Article 63(2) with respect to a detainee under the former Article 63 is pending at the time this Act enters into force, the former provisions shall apply.
Article 8 (Transitional measures concerning requests for temporary release from detention)
(1) Where a request for temporary release from detention has been filed with the head of the competent Regional Immigration Service under the former Article 65(1) at the time this Act enters into force, the former provisions shall apply.
(2) Where the former provisions apply under paragraph (1), no request for temporary release from detention may be filed again with the Immigration Detention Review Committee with respect to the same matters.

